:: t0_day01_hub_evening [home]
<<run SOY.Quests.complete('t0_day01', 'baseline')>>
<<run SOY.Time.ensureSlot(2)>>
<<run SOY.Locations.travel('street')>>
<<scene "mood/october-evening-walk" "Walking home in the October dusk, a paper bag under one arm">>

The sky is the color of a bruise when I come out of 814 Ninth Street. Purple and yellow at the edges, going dark. October evenings arrive sudden and non-negotiable.

My head is full. Overfull. Transfer methods. Clone designations. The 72-hour window. Elena Cordero's voice cutting through the information like a scalpel through gauze, clean and deliberate and slightly terrifying and Rafael's ninety minutes of questions, peeling me open layer by layer like he was looking for a specific organ and he'd know it when he found it.

I need food. I need beer. I need Chipi on my chest. But first I need to walk past something normal.

<<opt "t0_day01_evening_bodega" "Take the long way home and stop at Lulu's" "Rice, beans, and whatever she decides I need.">>
<<opt "t0_day01_dannys_scene" "Danny's Ramen" "A counter seat and K-pop too loud to think over.">>
<<opt "t0_day01_arrive_home" "Straight home" "Chipi's been alone eleven hours.">>


:: t0_day01_evening_bodega [home]
<<scene "locations/lulus-bodega" "Lulu's at dusk, warm light spilling onto the dark sidewalk">>
<<run SOY.Economy.spend(12, 'food')>>
<<set $npcs.lulu.lastSeen = $calendar.day>>
<<run SOY.NPCs.adjustRelationship('lulu', 1)>>
<<run SOY.Quests.completeSide('sq_004_bodega', 'visit')>>
<<run SOY.Quests.completeSide('sq_001_feed', 'eat')>>

The bells on the door. She looks up from her newspaper, different section now, she's made progress through the day.

<<say "Lulu">>Ay, mijo, you look like you've seen a ghost.<</say>>
<<say "Me">>Long day.<</say>>
<<say "Lulu">>Was the science good?<</say>>
<<say "Me">>The science was... a lot.<</say>>

She studies me the way she studies the newspaper, like she's going to find meaning if she looks hard enough. Then she puts down her magnifying glass and starts filling a bag without being asked. Rice. Beans. Two Modelos and the empanadas, different ones from this morning, chicken and green chile.

<<say "Me">>How much?<</say>>
<<say "Lulu">>Twelve dollars and you eat all of it, you hear me? You're too skinny. Your mother would be ashamed.<</say>>
<<say "Me">>My mother is four thousand miles away.<</say>>
<<say "Lulu">>God is closer.<</say>>

She touches her crucifix.

<<say "Lulu">>And God agrees with me. Eat.<</say>>

I pay. She pats my hand on the counter again, that quick warm pressure. I leave with the bag against my chest, the warmth of the empanadas bleeding through the paper and into my ribs.

<<opt "t0_day01_arrive_home" "Head home">>
<<if not visited("t0_day01_dannys_scene")>>
<<opt "t0_day01_dannys_option" "Actually, keep walking" "The apartment is going to be quiet. I need noise.">>
<</if>>


:: t0_day01_dannys_option [home]
I should go home. I have empanadas and Modelo and a 340-page PDF to read and a cat who's keeping a detailed log of my absences.

But the apartment is going to be quiet and the quiet is going to fill up with Elena's voice and Rafael's questions and the number twenty-seven and I need noise. Specific noise. The kind that comes from a counter seat in a ramen shop with the K-pop turned up too loud.

Danny's is six blocks east. The neon sign in the window says "DANNY'S" in pink and "ラーメン" in blue and the door handle is always slightly greasy and the entire place smells like pork bone broth and sesame and whatever Danny's burning in the back that might be incense and might be a mistake.

<<opt "t0_day01_dannys_scene" "Go to Danny's">>
<<opt "t0_day01_arrive_home" "Go home instead">>


:: t0_day01_arrive_home
<<if not visited("t0_day01_senora_vidal") and SOY.Random.check(40)>>
<<goto "t0_day01_senora_vidal">>
<<else>>
<<goto "t0_day01_evening_home">>
<</if>>


:: t0_day01_evening_home [home]
<<run SOY.Locations.travel('apartment')>>
<<run SOY.Quests.complete('t0_day01', 'go_home')>>
<<scene "mood/apartment-night-couch" "The apartment at night, phone-glow on the cat">>

<<if visited("t0_day01_evening_home") lte 1>>
Chipi is at the door. Not near the door. At the door. Sitting in the exact center of the doormat, staring at the doorknob like she's been counting the seconds since I left and has opinions about every single one.

<<say "Me">>Hola, gatita.<</say>>

She meows. Not the hungry meow. The offended meow. The "I have been alone for eleven hours and I want you to know that I noticed" meow.

I drop my bag on the counter. Feed her the expensive salmon. She forgives me in approximately four seconds, which is her usual grace period. The sound of her eating fills the kitchen, tiny wet crunching that would be disgusting from any other creature but from Chipi is somehow the most comforting sound in my apartment.

I crack a Modelo. Pour it into a glass because I'm not an animal. I am a man who stands at his kitchen counter in a navy henley drinking beer from a glass and eating empanadas while his cat eats fish on the floor and the apartment is quiet. Not peaceful quiet.

The kind of quiet where the walls hold the day's noise and play it back in fragments. Elena's voice,

<<say "Elena">>The body is a vessel. Consciousness is the pilot. The vessel has its own momentum.<</say>>

Rafael's pen on his clipboard. The scratch of it. The pauses where he waited and I squirmed and he watched me squirm with the patience of a man who's seen a thousand people squirm and finds each one individually interesting.

I eat the empanadas standing up. Chicken and green chile. Lulu doesn't mess around. The heat sits on my tongue and then slides down my throat and settles in my stomach next to the beer and the anxiety.

My phone is on the counter. I should call Paco. I should. He's the one who sent me to that door. He deserves to know what was on the other side.
<<else>>
Back inside. The Modelo's gone warm on the counter. Chipi reclaims my lap without asking.
<</if>>

<<if not visited("t0_day01_paco_call")>>
<<opt "t0_day01_paco_call" "Call Paco" "He deserves to know what was on the other side.">>
<</if>>
<<if not visited("t0_day01_evening_cook")>>
<<opt "t0_day01_evening_cook" "Eat first, call later" "Rice and beans. My mother's recipe, more or less.">>
<</if>>
<<opt "t0_day01_evening_phone" "Check phone messages">>
<<if not visited("t0_day01_handbook_reading")>>
<<opt "t0_day01_handbook_reading" "Open the handbook PDF" "Three hundred and forty pages. Chapter one.">>
<</if>>
<<opt "t0_day01_sleep" "Go to bed">>
<<if $settings.showExplicit and not visited("t0_day01_solo_night")>>
<<opt "t0_day01_solo_night" "Lie down, the body has other ideas" "Explicit. It's been over a week.">>
<</if>>


:: t0_day01_evening_cook [home]
<<run SOY.Quests.completeSide('sq_001_feed', 'eat')>>

Rice and beans. My mother's recipe, or the approximation I've reverse-engineered from her voice notes over four years. She doesn't measure anything. //Un poquito de esto, mijo.// A little of this. A little of that. Three cloves of garlic but small ones, or two but big. Cumin until it smells right. She cooks by feel and I cook by trying to feel what she feels from four thousand miles away.

The rice goes in the pot. I add water, too much, I always add too much, the rice will be soft instead of fluffy and my mother would know instantly and forgive me instantly and tell me to add more garlic next time.

While the rice cooks I sit at the kitchen table. It's a two-person table from IKEA that I assembled drunk by myself on my first night in this apartment. One leg is slightly shorter than the others. I've had a folded napkin under it for three years. The second chair has never been used by anyone who wasn't Chipi.

Chipi jumps up now. Sits in the second chair. Looks at me across the table like we're about to have a conversation she's been putting off.

<<say "Me">>I'm going to be transferring my consciousness into women's bodies for money. Thoughts?<</say>>

She blinks slowly.

<<say "Me">>Yeah. Me too.<</say>>

The rice timer goes off. I make a plate. Sit down. Eat at the table because sitting is supposed to be better for digestion or mental health or both, and I could use help with both.

The food is okay. Rice is too soft. Beans are good. I eat all of it because Lulu told me to and because I'm hungry in a way that isn't just about food. I'm hungry for something to feel solid, and a full stomach is close enough.

<<opt "t0_day01_evening_home" "Back to the couch">>


:: t0_day01_evening_couch [home]
Second Modelo. I drink it slower. Chipi stretches across my lap, all four legs extended, purring like a small engine. The TV is off. I don't turn it on. The quiet has a different quality tonight. Not the hostile quiet of the last few weeks, the "you're alone and everything is falling apart" quiet. This is more like a pause. The held breath between one thing ending and another beginning.

I think about Elena's lecture. The three transfer methods, pod, headset, sleep capsule. The way she described the sensation of transfer. //Thermal shift, perceptual compression, expansion.// Like being pushed through a needle's eye and coming out the other side larger. Or at least different.

I think about Rafael's questions. The way he asked about dating. //Single. Four years.// He wrote something down and I wanted to see what he wrote because I've been narrating my own loneliness for so long that someone else's version of it felt like it might be more accurate. Or at least more concise.

I think about tomorrow. Module 1 continues. The first tomorrow, someone is going to put my brain into a woman's body and I'm going to walk around in it and feel things I've never felt and then come back and be expected to debrief about it with a Brazilian ex-military psychologist who can read me like a receipt.

The beer is empty. Chipi is asleep. My phone screen says 11:17 PM.

<<say "Me">>Tomorrow.<</say>>

I say it to the dark apartment. Nobody answers. That's fine. I'm used to that.

<<opt "t0_day01_sleep" "Go to bed">>


:: t0_day01_handbook_reading [home]
<<set $flags.handbook_read = true>>

I open the PDF on my phone. Lie on the bed. Chipi sits on my chest, which means I'm reading the screen at an angle past her head, which means I'm getting cat hair on my phone and not retaining much of anything, but I try.

<h2>Chapter 1 - Foundations of Neuroelectric Identity Mapping</h2>

<div class="quote">The human consciousness is not localized. While the brain serves as the primary processing center, the complete cognitive-emotional-somatic identity extends throughout the entire nervous system. A person's identity is as much in their fingertips as in their frontal lobe, touch memory, proprioceptive habit, the physical patterns of a lifetime of living in one specific body. Transfer technology maps all of it.</div>

I read three pages. Chipi falls asleep on my chest. Her weight is warm and small and specific, maybe three kilograms of cat pressing me into the mattress. In a few hours she'll be the only thing pressing me into anything because I'll be in a transfer pod getting my consciousness pulled through a needle's eye into a body that weighs more than Chipi but less than me.

I close the PDF. Battery at 23%. Tomorrow.

I set the phone on the nightstand and lie there in the dark with the cat on my chest and the handbook half-read and the day sitting on top of me like a second blanket, heavy, warm, and impossible to kick off.

<<opt "t0_day01_sleep" "Let the day close">>
<<opt "t0_day01_evening_home" "Actually, get back up">>


:: t0_day01_sleep
<<if $calendar.day is 1>>
	<<run SOY.Time.ensureSlot(3)>>
	<<run SOY.Time.advance()>>
	<<run SOY.Body.decayPhantoms()>>
<</if>>
<<run SOY.Locations.travel('apartment')>>

Teeth. Face. Lights off.

The bed. Queen-size, bought on sale at a furniture outlet three and a half years ago because it was cheap and I was optimistic and I thought maybe, at some point, someone would be in it besides me and a cat. That hasn't happened. The bed is too big. It's always too big. I sleep on the left side because the right side has Chipi and a pillow I don't use and the ghost of a person I haven't met yet.

Chipi settles against my hip. Her warmth is small and specific. I put my hand on her back. She purrs. The vibration moves through my hand into my wrist and up my arm and I feel it in my chest, this tiny engine of aliveness pressed against my body in the dark.

I close my eyes. The day replays in fragments.

<<say "Yuki">>Room 4. Don't be late.<</say>>

<<say "Elena">>The body is a vessel. Consciousness is the pilot.<</say>>

<<say "Rafael">>How long have you been single?<</say>>

Four years.

<<say "Rafael">>Dating?<</say>>

Hard to date when your residence is conditional.

<<say "Lulu">>God watches, Manuel.<</say>>

<<say "Paco">>You're not going home.<</say>>

<<say "James">>You deserve good things.<</say>>

The fragments blur. My breathing slows. Chipi's purr gets quieter or I get further away from it, I'm not sure which.

Twenty-seven days. The bed is too big. Tomorrow they're going to teach me more about what it means to be inside a body that isn't mine. Tonight I'm lying in my own body in my own bed in an apartment I might not have in a month, and the last thing I hear before sleep takes me is Chipi's purr and the radiator clicking on and the distant sound of a bus on Ninth Street going somewhere I'm not.

<<opt "t0_day02_wake" "Let sleep take me">>
